Falsifies `usb::verification::two_reports_produce_a_bounded_number_of_events`.

The defect: `changes` emits a release before every modifier transition, as a debounce. The bound of twenty is
the exact maximum (8 modifiers, 6 releases, 6 presses), so only a doubling bug can exceed it, and a
flip of every modifier bit now costs sixteen events.

Expected to fail: the harness's `assert!(n <= 20)`.

diff --git a/crates/usb/src/boot_keyboard.rs b/crates/usb/src/boot_keyboard.rs
index d18aee536..c7cfeabd9 100644
--- a/crates/usb/src/boot_keyboard.rs
+++ b/crates/usb/src/boot_keyboard.rs
@@ -96,2 +96,3 @@ pub fn changes(before: &BootReport, after: &BootReport, event: &mut dyn FnMut(u1
         if flipped & (1 << bit) != 0 {
+            event(code, false);
             event(code, after.modifiers & (1 << bit) != 0);
